{{fbdoc item="title" value="UNLOCK"}}----
Releases a file range lock

{{fbdoc item="syntax"}}##
	**Unlock** #//filenum//, //record//
	**Unlock** #//filenum//, //start// To //end//
##
{{fbdoc item="param"}}
	##//filenum//##
		The file number used to ##[[KeyPgOpen|Open]]## the file.
	##//record//##
		The record (##[[KeyPgRandom|Random]]## files) to unlock.
	##//start//##
		The first byte position (##[[KeyPgBinary|Binary]]## files) in a range to unlock.
	##//end//##
		The last byte position (##[[KeyPgBinary|Binary]]## files) in a range to unlock.

{{fbdoc item="desc"}}
	##**Unlock**## releases the byte or record range locked by ##[[KeyPgLock|Lock]]##. The first and final positions are inclusive.
	
	Use the same arguments as the matching ##[[KeyPgLock|Lock]]##. On Unix-like systems, file locks are advisory. Native unlock failures set a file I/O error, and targets without native byte-range locking report the operation as unsupported.

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}
		 For an example see ##[[KeyPgLock|Lock]]##.

{{fbdoc item="diff"}}
	- A single position or explicit range is required; the entire file cannot be unlocked implicitly

{{fbdoc item="see"}}
	- ##[[KeyPgLock|Lock]]##
	- ##[[KeyPgOpen|Open]]##
	- ##[[KeyPgScreenunlock|ScreenUnlock]]##

